From a0ba2858d047b3cfb758b96c5e9b62020de187ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:28:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kanban notifier: skip an unchanged board's collect pass on a
 full recovery key (H1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The gateway notifier ran collect_board on every board every 5 s (3.1% of a core on the hub) although 9 of 10
boards had no content change in 600 s. A board's pass is now skipped only when all of these hold:
- its key equals the key read before the last full pass: the activity revision, a digest of the
  kanban_notify_subs bookkeeping the revision ignores (inflight_*, last_event_id, last_ping_event_id), and what
  this gateway serves (platforms, profiles, adapter objects, profile routes, legacy-row ownership), so an adapter
  reconnecting or a route appearing re-runs every board;
- that pass listed no pending sub (C10: a pending sub left unclaimed for want of an adapter, anchor or TUI owner
  keeps the board running every tick);
- no in-flight claim on the board (orphan/stale-claim recovery, NOTIFY_CLAIM_STALE_S, stays on the 5 s tick);
- the hourly GC is not due, and the last full pass is under 60 s old.

list_notify_subs(pending_only) also takes pending_kinds: a row whose only unseen events are kinds its claim never
reads (heartbeats, spawned, ...) is no longer listed every tick to claim nothing, so idle running cards let the
gate close.

Replay benchmark (hub snapshot of 10 boards, chg1 change rates, 120 ticks): collect CPU 79.5 -> 33.8 ms/tick
(1.59% -> 0.68% of a core at 5 s); with a 434 MB pinned WAL 83.5 -> 30.8 ms (1.67% -> 0.62%).

Card t_01a1d59e598f6a06 (design t_01a1d563324d7e8e §3 H1, review R4).
